comments.body:
That is good news, @JhonatanFelix. :) Thanks for following up.
I won't test it now, since I don't have the nerves right now to figure out how to test an unreleased debugpy in my cursor, but I'm happy there is a fix.

@jeremiedbb: You're right, this bug does not appear on #33941 with my current debugpy version (1.8.20).

I think it would be neat to get this display with `plot_method="contour"` to behave as follows:

- for all response methods, always get contours at the class boundaries for any 2 pairs of classes (but I don't know how to do this);
- for the continuous response methods (`predict_proba` and `decision_function`) add contour lines for different levels with different color intensities **in addition to** the class boundaries contour lines.
